{
  "metadata": {
    "note": "The UI/Android agent tooling declared for the author's three machines (dasik-personal-config: common/ai-skills.json, common/mcp-servers.json, common/codex-files.json, android-cli in common/packages.json), copied verbatim minus the entries vm-ai-skills*.json and vm-mcp.json already cover. For the QEMU VM harness (scripts/vmtest/qemu.sh install-driven, then drive with guest-agent-ui-tooling.sh). NOT for real hardware. The agent CLIs come from PACKAGES here, as on the real machines (openai-codex from extra, claude-code from the AUR), so the INSTALL converges both domains in the chroot — the reinstall path — and the guest script then drives every verb day-2. Needs NETWORK in the guest.",
    "resources": "DASIK_VM_RAM=4096 DASIK_VM_DISK=16G DASIK_VM_INSTALL_TIMEOUT=3600 DASIK_VM_DRIVE_TIMEOUT=3600: 36 `npx skills add` runs (one clone each) and two AUR builds. Chromium is deliberately absent: registering chrome-devtools does not need it, and it would double the disk.",
    "codex_login": "`codex login` is interactive and ties the machine to an account, so the guest never has one. The codex half of the 21st plugin is measured, not assumed: guest-agent-ui-tooling.sh reports whether `codex plugin add 21st@21st-dev` works without it."
  },
  "disks": {
    "disks": [
      {
        "device": "/dev/vda",
        "partition_table": "gpt",
        "wipe_disk": false,
        "partitions": [
          {
            "label": "ESP",
            "size": "512MiB",
            "filesystem": "fat32",
            "partition_type": "esp",
            "mountpoint": "/boot",
            "format": true
          },
          {
            "label": "ROOT",
            "size": "rest",
            "filesystem": "ext4",
            "partition_type": "linux",
            "mountpoint": "/",
            "format": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
